cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the paper as below."
type: software
title: "Virtual spatial transcriptomics links kidney histopathology to disease-associated molecular programs"
abstract: "Analysis code and data for the paper. DeepSpot-M predicts the spatially resolved expression of 19,338 genes from H&E whole-slide images of kidney biopsies. It was benchmarked against measured 10x Visium in held-out biopsies of the Kidney Precision Medicine Project (KPMP) and applied to 1,534 whole-slide images of 476 KPMP participants, giving a virtual spatial transcriptomics atlas of the human kidney, validated with 10x Xenium and in rat kidney injury (Open TG-GATEs)."
